#* {{quote-book|en|year=1953|title=Nature Magazine  |author= |page=223 |ISBN= |passage=After removal from a worker bee they should be '''potashed''' in ten percent potassium hydroxide, washed, dehydrated, cleared, and mounted. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|title=Senckenbergiana biologica  |author= |page=136 |ISBN= |passage=For the extraction of the internal sclerites the aedeagus was '''potashed''' in cold saturated KOH solution for several hours and transferred to a vial of distilled water.  }}

